         0, "Generation interval (L) is the average age of parents when their replacement offspring are born. Because annual rate of genetic improvement is Delta_G / year = R / L, prolonging the generation interval directly reduces the annual rate of genetic progress unless offset by much higher accuracy or intensity.",
